# The command line fits its measurements and says how it went. `fit` makes the sum `Fit | Failed` in one of two arms
# (its early return is the one arm, what follows the other), and one copairing takes it apart where it arises:
# `describe` matches it and builds a Report in either arm, which the command line prints.

route fits.cli.main
step main/fit
choice main/fit/?1
step main/fit/?1/Failed()
known #130 step main/fit/?1/Fit()                                  # what follows the early return is the other arm
step main/describe
choice main/describe/?1
step main/describe/?1/Report()
step main/describe/?1/Report()#2

line entry > main call
line main/fit/?1/Failed() > Failed@main/fit/?1 value
known #130 line main/fit/?1/Fit() > Fit@main/fit/?1 value
line Failed@main/fit/?1 > main/fit value                           # fit hands back what either arm made
known #130 line Fit@main/fit/?1 > main/fit value
line main/fit > Fit | Failed@main/fit value                        # fit gives one value, the sum
line Fit | Failed@main/fit > main/describe value                   # the match in describe's own body opens it
line main/describe/?1/Report() > Report@main/describe/?1 value
line main/describe/?1/Report()#2 > Report@main/describe/?1 value
line Report@main/describe/?1 > main/describe value
line main/describe > Report·report@main/describe value
known #101 line Report·report@main/describe > main value            # main prints the line and the points
line main > Screen own

home Failed@main/fit/?1 main/fit
known #130 home Fit@main/fit/?1 main/fit
home Fit | Failed@main/fit main
home Report@main/describe/?1 main/describe
home Report·report@main/describe main

side entry left
side Screen right

# the early return is read as a choice of one arm, and what follows it as a step after the choice
known #130 extra step main/fit/Fit()
known #130 extra line main/fit/Fit() > Fit@main/fit/Fit() value
known #130 extra line Fit@main/fit/Fit() > main/fit value
known #130 extra home Fit@main/fit/Fit() main/fit

# fit hands on, beside the sum it gives, each of its variants as a value of its own
known #132 extra line main/fit > Failed@main/fit value
known #132 extra line main/fit > Fit@main/fit value
known #132 extra line Failed@main/fit > main/describe value
known #132 extra line Fit@main/fit > main/describe value
known #132 extra home Failed@main/fit main
known #132 extra home Fit@main/fit main
